{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md at exact fa6417e66c87a8a16e507373ed65b23d02d710ba on request/scope-contract-r13, under promise git:sha1…7ae010b on request git:sha1…d156340\n\nScope and replay contract, revision 14 at fa6417e66c87a8a16e507373ed65b23d02d710ba on request/scope-contract-r13 (three commits on adopted revision 13, 86c6aabd), for request 10e7093d. All four subjects; the lane companion and the admission read inventory are unchanged. Decisions. (1) R1-53: three inputs (an act, an outcome, a delivery of a result) may hold an optional member observed, a list of observation uses; two tagged kinds are added for membership and rules observations; each gets the guards of a grant's observation; the heads retained for one subject never go back (mismatch observation-older); only platform code writes one. Only an entry that retains such an observation changes bytes. (2) R1-54: what travels beside an intent gains values: canonical JSON matched by digest in the domain a stated place of a platform act names; no new byte domain; retained once per domain and digest and never redactable; no value travels beside a message. (3) Witness 18.18: the 116 KiB cases now say they omit the optional merge, and two new cases count it (156 KiB) and keep it in uses of a written refusal; a written entry keeps every foreign entry fetched for its input. (4) Reading another scope's entry: a reader applies none of its own types; a foreign field is the raw value in the bytes; the mark there is a record and equals no fact reference; a number from another scope's entry is no item of the reader. Depth in replay counts the chain from the target in both phases. The later I2 entries DP1 to DP5 and DR1 to DR15 are disposed: with the 165, 185 entries. The must-change list has 23 rows, 20 owed; three are new (a foreign number is no item; an own request with no name is read raw; a written refusal lists every fetched entry). Open points R1-53 and R1-54 are closed; R1-55 (the members of the two new observation kinds, which are my reading of the authority note's prose) and R1-56 (four recovery seams) are new. Two things asked of the authority note's owner: the order-of-heads guard is stricter than its rule G10 in one case; and that note says two things about which entry records dispatched. The author's adversarial re-read changed three passages and is recorded in the corrections file. Reading coverage, stated in the note: the authority note revision 16 was read in sections 3.3, 6.5, 12.1.8 and every row citing P19, P21 or P18 by the author, and the rest by four delegated readers; the recovery design revision 4 by one delegated reader, in part; the I2 source at 58465dbf in the named functions; no test; the authority note's revision 17 and 18 were not read. The I2 source is stated as under review and not accepted (it has since been approved at 77555943 and is landing). Design only: nothing was run.","body":{"commit":"fa6417e66c87a8a16e507373ed65b23d02d710ba","path":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md"}}